    {"id":"la-degustation","cat":"berth","tier":"berth_top","priority":1,"name":"La Degustation Bohême Bourgeoise","short":"La Degustation","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Haštalská, the lanes behind St Agnes","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=La+Degustation+Boh%C3%AAme+Bourgeoise+Praha","badge":"STAR","tags":["Tasting menu 3,500 CZK; pairings 2,000 / 3,700 CZK, non-alcoholic 1,300 CZK (own menu page, Sept 2026)","Online via the site; 1-3 weeks ahead for dinner.","Dinner"],"productTags":["czech canon","tasting menu","local sourcing"],"hours":"Mon-Sun 11:30-15:00, 18:00-00:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"When it opened in 2006, the Ambiente group's line was simple: 'we cook Czech cuisine because we understand it best'. La Degustation turned trout and dill, rabbit and carrot, venison and forest mushrooms into a tasting menu framed as 'a tribute to the Czech landscape and those who cultivate it'. Oldřich Sahajdák oversees; Marco Christov runs the kitchen. It kept its star in the first Czech guide.","address":"Haštalská 18, Praha 1","phone":"+420 733 332 771","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.091032,"lng":14.425106,"category":"creme","subcat":"LA CRÈME","hook":"Czech cooking as a tasting menu, 99 per cent of it bought within 250 kilometres.","person":"Oldřich Sahajdák (chef patron) · Marco Christov (executive chef)","signature":"The six-course 'Czech landscape' tasting menu","verdict":"The room that taught Prague to be proud of Czech food; still the most Czech of the stars.","caveat":"Tasting menu only; pairings nearly double the bill.","price_range":"Tasting menu 3,500 CZK; pairings 2,000 / 3,700 CZK, non-alcoholic 1,300 CZK (own menu page, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online via the site; 1-3 weeks ahead for dinner.","best_time":"Dinner","dishes":[{"name":"Tomato, onion, basil","note":"The opener: late-summer Bohemian garden."},{"name":"Trout, dill, cucumber","note":"Dill is the Czech herb; koprovka in miniature."},{"name":"Rabbit, carrot, courgette","note":"Farmyard Bohemia."},{"name":"Venison, mushrooms, rosemary","note":"The forest course; Czechs forage mushrooms as a national sport."},{"name":"Yoghurt, blueberry, thyme","note":"Blueberries from the woods, not a farm."},{"name":"Grape soda","note":"The closing sip, a nod to Moravian vineyards."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN ★ 2025","full":"One MICHELIN Star, MICHELIN Guide Czechia 2025 (retained)","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, 11 Dec 2025"},"charter":{"price":"3,500 CZK per head, pairings 1,300-3,700 CZK (own site, Sept 2026)","book":"1-3 weeks ahead online; groups by email boheme@ambi.cz","dress":"Smart casual (not stated; our reading)","warn":"Fixed tasting menu only: no à la carte for a picky guest","fit":"None; an intimate brick-and-wood interior · Private room: Private dining offered through booking; size not published"},"web":"https://ladegustation.ambi.cz/"},
    {"id":"papilio","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":8,"name":"Restaurant Papilio","short":"Papilio","neighborhood":"Vysoký Újezd · village near the Brdy forest, about 20 minutes' drive from Prague","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Restaurant+Papilio+Vysok%C3%BD+%C3%9Ajezd","badge":"2 STARS","tags":["8 courses 5,500 CZK; 10 courses 6,500 CZK; pairings extra (own site, Sept 2026)","Online at the site or +420 724 132 013; book well ahead since the second star.","Thursday-Saturday lunch"],"productTags":["two stars","chef's counter","day trip"],"hours":"Wed dinner from 18:30; Thu-Sat lunch 12:00-15:30 and dinner from 18:30 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"In December 2025 MICHELIN gave its only Czech two-star not to a city room but to Jan Knedla's counter in a renovated building in Vysoký Újezd, beside a golf course outside Prague. A Czech guide describes French precision, Asian refinement and local ingredients. Ten courses at the counter, with a tea pairing for anyone not drinking wine.","address":"Tyršova náves 1, 267 16 Vysoký Újezd","phone":"+420 724 132 013","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":49.993134,"lng":14.205624,"category":"creme","subcat":"LA CRÈME","hook":"The only two-star in the country — a chef's counter in a village, not a Prague dining room.","person":"Jan Knedla (chef)","signature":"The ten-course menu at the counter","verdict":"The highest-rated table in Czechia, and worth the drive for anyone who counts stars.","caveat":"Outside the city: taxi or driver there and back; closed Sun-Tue.","price_range":"8 courses 5,500 CZK; 10 courses 6,500 CZK; pairings extra (own site, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online at the site or +420 724 132 013; book well ahead since the second star.","best_time":"Thursday-Saturday lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Ten-course menu","note":"6,500 CZK."},{"name":"Eight-course menu","note":"5,500 CZK."},{"name":"Tea pairing","note":"The alternative to wine, listed by Czech guides."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN ★★ 2025","full":"Two MICHELIN Stars, new, MICHELIN Guide Czechia 2025 (the only two-star in the country)","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, 11 Dec 2025"},"charter":{"price":"5,500 CZK (8 courses) or 6,500 CZK (10 courses) per head before drinks (own site, Sept 2026)","book":"As early as possible, online or by phone; lunch is easier","dress":"Smart; not stated","warn":"A 20-minute drive each way; closed Sun-Tue","fit":"Countryside village; the counter faces the kitchen · Private room: Chef's counter format; buyout not published, ask"},"web":"http://restaurant-papilio.cz/"},
    {"id":"taro","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":9,"name":"TARO","short":"Taro","neighborhood":"Nové Město · Dunaj palace on Národní třída","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Taro+restaurant+N%C3%A1rodn%C3%AD+Praha","badge":"RISING","tags":["Tasting menu; price not published online (Sept 2026)","Online via Tableo; call for same-day seats.","Early seating at the bar"],"productTags":["vietnamese-czech","counter","young chef"],"hours":"Tue-Sat 17:30-23:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Khanh and Giang Ta started Taro in Anděl and in 2025 moved it into the Dunaj palace on Národní, darker and more elegant. Next door they opened Paté, a French-Asian bakery. In December 2025 MICHELIN named Khanh Ta its Young Chef of the year, for dishes that balance complexity with ease. The counter seats around the open kitchen are made for a solo diner.","address":"Národní 10, Praha 1","phone":"+420 777 446 007","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.081538,"lng":14.416735,"category":"rising","subcat":"THE NEW WAVE","hook":"Two Vietnamese-Czech brothers at a kitchen bar on Národní; one was MICHELIN's Young Chef of 2025.","person":"Khanh Ta and Giang Ta","signature":"The tasting dinner at the kitchen bar","verdict":"The most likely next star in Prague.","caveat":"Menu and prices not published on the site this month.","price_range":"Tasting menu; price not published online (Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online via Tableo; call for same-day seats.","best_time":"Early seating at the bar","dishes":[{"name":"Tasting menu","note":"Vietnamese technique, Czech produce."},{"name":"Congee breakfast at Paté next door","note":"The brothers' bakery, the cheap way into the same kitchen thinking."},{"name":"Banh mi at Paté","note":"French bread, Vietnamese filling, Prague address."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Young Chef 2025","full":"MICHELIN Young Chef Award 2025 to Khanh Ta","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide Czechia, 11 Dec 2025"},"web":"https://www.taro.cz/"},
    {"id":"marie-b","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":10,"name":"Marie B","short":"Marie B","neighborhood":"Staré Město · through a graffiti courtyard on Dlouhá","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Marie+B+Dlouh%C3%A1+Praha","badge":"COUNTER","tags":["Tasting 2,150 CZK; pairings 1,300-3,000 CZK, non-alcoholic 900 CZK (own site, Sept 2026)","Online; counter seats go a week or two ahead.","Late seating"],"productTags":["carte blanche","moravian wine","counter"],"hours":"Daily 17:30-24:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"You reach it through a graffiti courtyard into a 14th-century townhouse, sit at a horseshoe counter round the kitchen, and eat a carte blanche that changes daily; the dishes are named only after you have eaten them. It takes its name from Marie B. Svobodová, whose cookbook of 1894 is on display, and its manager, Zdeněk Oudes, won MICHELIN's Sommelier Award in 2025.","address":"Dlouhá 37, Praha 1","phone":"+420 737 595 913","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.090787,"lng":14.426733,"category":"rising","subcat":"THE NEW WAVE","hook":"No menu: a U-shaped counter in a 14th-century house, and you learn what you ate afterwards.","person":"Oldřich Sahajdák (chef patron) · Pavol Oľha (head chef) · Zdeněk Oudes (sommelier)","signature":"Carte blanche menu with the Moravian pairing","verdict":"Starred-kitchen thinking for 2,150 CZK; the best-value serious dinner in the Old Town.","caveat":"No choice at all; declare allergies when booking.","price_range":"Tasting 2,150 CZK; pairings 1,300-3,000 CZK, non-alcoholic 900 CZK (own site, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online; counter seats go a week or two ahead.","best_time":"Late seating","dishes":[{"name":"Carte blanche tasting","note":"Changes daily; dishes revealed after you eat them."},{"name":"Moravian wine pairing","note":"From the Sommelier Award winner."},{"name":"Vin de Marie","note":"The wine bar in the same building, for a glass without dinner."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Sommelier 2025","full":"MICHELIN Sommelier Award 2025 to Zdeněk Oudes; MICHELIN Selected","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide Czechia, 11 Dec 2025"},"web":"https://marieb.ambi.cz/"},
    {"id":"benjamin","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":11,"name":"Benjamin","short":"Benjamin","neighborhood":"Vršovice · Norská, a residential street off the Vinohrady edge","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Benjamin+Norsk%C3%A1+14+Praha","badge":"COUNTER","tags":["Top MICHELIN band (€€€€); price not confirmed this month","Direct with the restaurant; weeks ahead.","The single evening sitting"],"productTags":["10 seats","czech","counter"],"hours":"Tue-Sat 18:45-22:30; Sun-Mon closed (MICHELIN listing, 2025-26)","why":"The cooks serve you across the counter themselves, one sitting a night, one menu of eight courses. MICHELIN calls the food carefully executed and boldly flavoured, rooted in Czech tradition and sourced entirely from local producers, and places it in its top price band without a star. Book it for two: ten seats round a horseshoe do not suit a group of six.","address":"Norská 14, Praha 10","phone":"+420 774 141 432","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.07177,"lng":14.455523,"category":"rising","subcat":"THE NEW WAVE","hook":"Ten seats round a horseshoe counter, one eight-course Czech menu, one sitting a night.","signature":"The eight-course counter menu","verdict":"The most intimate serious dinner in the city; book it for two, not six.","caveat":"Ten seats: miss the booking and there is no walk-in.","price_range":"Top MICHELIN band (€€€€); price not confirmed this month","reservation":"Direct with the restaurant; weeks ahead.","best_time":"The single evening sitting","dishes":[{"name":"Eight-course seasonal menu","note":"Czech tradition, local produce only."},{"name":"Wine pairing","note":"Optional."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Selected","full":"MICHELIN Selected, Guide Czechia 2025","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, Dec 2025"},"web":"https://www.benjamin14.cz/"},
    {"id":"terasa-u-zlate-studne","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":13,"name":"Terasa U Zlaté studně","short":"Terasa","neighborhood":"Malá Strana · rooftop of the Golden Well hotel under the castle","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Terasa+U+Zlat%C3%A9+studn%C4%9B+Praha","badge":"VIEW","tags":["Seasonal tasting menu; prices not published online (Sept 2026)","Phone or restaurant@goldenwell.cz; terrace tables go first.","Sunset in season"],"productTags":["rooftop","castle view","tasting menu"],"hours":"Not published on the site (Sept 2026); call","why":"The terrace of the Golden Well hotel hangs at the top of Malá Strana, with the roofs and the Old Town spread out below. It won Pavel Maurer's Grand Restaurant — judged by volunteer secret diners — three times, the last in 2019, and Gault&Millau gives Lukáš Hlaváček's kitchen three toques. It is the view dinner where the food is not an afterthought.","address":"U Zlaté studně 166/4, Praha 1","phone":"+420 257 533 322","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.090965,"lng":14.404495,"category":"houses","subcat":"THE GRAND HOUSES","hook":"A terrace dinner under the castle, over the red roofs of Malá Strana — with a serious kitchen.","person":"Lukáš Hlaváček (head chef)","signature":"Seasonal tasting menu on the terrace","verdict":"If a guest wants the castle-and-roofs view with dinner, this is the one worth the money.","caveat":"Hours and prices not published; the terrace is weather-dependent.","price_range":"Seasonal tasting menu; prices not published online (Sept 2026)","reservation":"Phone or restaurant@goldenwell.cz; terrace tables go first.","best_time":"Sunset in season","dishes":[{"name":"Seasonal tasting menu","note":"The main format."},{"name":"Steak","note":"On the site's gallery; ask what is on."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Maurer winner x3","full":"Maurerův výběr Grand Restaurant, first place three times (last 2019); Gault&Millau three toques","cosign":"Maurerův výběr; Aktuálně.cz"},"charter":{"price":"Not published; ask for the tasting menu price (Sept 2026)","book":"2-3 weeks ahead for a terrace table; phone +420 257 533 322","dress":"Smart; not stated","warn":"The terrace is the point; in rain or cold you get the indoor room","fit":"Roofs of Malá Strana and the Old Town from under the castle · Private room: Yes: gala dinners and private events; size on request"},"web":"https://www.terasauzlatestudne.cz/"},
    {"id":"villa-richter","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":14,"name":"Villa Richter","short":"Villa Richter","neighborhood":"Hradčany · on the Old Castle Steps, in the St Wenceslas vineyard","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Villa+Richter+Praha","badge":"VINEYARD","tags":["Not published online (Sept 2026)","Phone or info@villarichter.cz.","Late afternoon, before sunset"],"productTags":["vineyard","castle view","events"],"hours":"Not published on the site (Sept 2026); call","why":"Villa Richter stands in the St Wenceslas vineyard below the castle, which tradition says the saint planted and the house says has made royal wine for more than a thousand years. The views run across the castle, Malá Strana and the centre. Today it is as much a wedding and festival venue as a restaurant, with its own harvest festival.","address":"Staré zámecké schody 6/251, Praha 1","phone":"+420 702 282 402","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.092524,"lng":14.408349,"category":"houses","subcat":"THE GRAND HOUSES","hook":"A glass of wine inside the vineyard said to have been planted by St Wenceslas himself.","signature":"A glass of the vineyard's own wine at the terrace rail","verdict":"Go for the vineyard and the view at aperitif hour; the food is not the reason.","caveat":"Event-heavy: check it is not booked out for a wedding.","price_range":"Not published online (Sept 2026)","reservation":"Phone or info@villarichter.cz.","best_time":"Late afternoon, before sunset","dishes":[{"name":"St Wenceslas vineyard wine","note":"The house draw; ask what is poured."},{"name":"Vinobraní harvest festival","note":"The house runs one; dates on its site."}],"web":"https://www.villarichter.cz/"},
    {"id":"v-zatisi","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":15,"name":"V Zátiší","short":"V Zátiší","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Liliová, by Bethlehem Square, three minutes from Charles Bridge","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=V+Z%C3%A1ti%C5%A1%C3%AD+Liliov%C3%A1+Praha","badge":"HOUSE","tags":["Summer festival menu 1,395 CZK for three courses with a drink pairing (own site, summer 2026); tasting and à la carte also","Online or phone; private rooms by email vzatisi@zatisigroup.cz.","Weekday lunch"],"productTags":["private rooms","since 1991","czech-slavic"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 11:30-15:00, 17:00-23:00; Sat-Sun brunch 11:30-15:00, dinner 17:00-23:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"V Zátiší's group says it is celebrating 35 years — which puts its start right after the Velvet Revolution, when private restaurants became legal again. Daniel Bureš cooks what he calls a modern reading of Slavic flavours, and the house is B Corp certified. Note the quarrel: its site calls it Michelin-starred; MICHELIN lists it as Selected, without a star.","address":"Liliová 1, Praha 1","phone":"+420 222 221 155","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.084382,"lng":14.416369,"category":"houses","subcat":"THE GRAND HOUSES","hook":"One of the first private fine-dining rooms after 1989, and the easiest private table in the Old Town.","person":"Daniel Bureš (chef)","signature":"The Czech-leaning tasting menu","verdict":"The practical grand room for a group: central, private rooms, open seven days.","caveat":"Its own site overstates its MICHELIN status.","price_range":"Summer festival menu 1,395 CZK for three courses with a drink pairing (own site, summer 2026); tasting and à la carte also","reservation":"Online or phone; private rooms by email vzatisi@zatisigroup.cz.","best_time":"Weekday lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Tasting menu","note":"Slavic flavours, modern treatment."},{"name":"Business lunch menu","note":"Weekdays."},{"name":"Weekend brunch","note":"Sat-Sun 11:30-15:00."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Selected","full":"MICHELIN Selected, Guide Czechia 2025 (the restaurant's own site claims a star; MICHELIN does not list one)","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, Dec 2025"},"charter":{"price":"Three-course festival menu with pairing 1,395 CZK (summer 2026); tasting menu on request","book":"1-2 weeks; private rooms 3-4 weeks ahead by email","dress":"Smart casual","warn":"Do not repeat its 'Michelin-starred' claim to a guest: it is MICHELIN Selected","fit":"Old Town lane; no river view · Private room: Yes: private and semi-private rooms for 10-40; buyout to 90"},"web":"https://www.vzatisi.cz/"},
    {"id":"kampa-park","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":16,"name":"Kampa Park","short":"Kampa Park","neighborhood":"Malá Strana · on Kampa island, the terrace at the foot of Charles Bridge","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kampa+Park+Praha","badge":"RIVER","tags":["Mains 995-1,695 CZK; vegetarian 695 CZK; caviar 5,550 CZK (own menu page, Sept 2026)","Online; terrace tables go first in summer.","Sunset, terrace season"],"productTags":["charles bridge","terrace","boat trips"],"hours":"Not published on the pages read (Sept 2026)","why":"Nils Jebens found Prague in 1994 and opened Kampa Park on the water beside the bridge, and the terrace has been the city's best-known expensive river table ever since. Honey-glazed duck is 995 CZK, Black Angus 1,695, fifty grams of caviar 5,550. The group also runs private Vltava trips with a captain.","address":"","phone":"+420 296 826 102","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.087404,"lng":14.409333,"category":"river","subcat":"ON THE VLTAVA","hook":"The Charles Bridge terrace since 1994: the most famous view table in Prague, priced for it.","person":"Nils Jebens (founder)","signature":"A terrace table facing Charles Bridge","verdict":"The spectacle version: book it for the bridge, not for the kitchen.","caveat":"Main courses near 1,000-1,700 CZK; no guide recognition this cycle.","price_range":"Mains 995-1,695 CZK; vegetarian 695 CZK; caviar 5,550 CZK (own menu page, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online; terrace tables go first in summer.","best_time":"Sunset, terrace season","dishes":[{"name":"Honey-glazed duck breast","note":"995 CZK."},{"name":"Rack of lamb","note":"1,295 CZK."},{"name":"Black Angus steak","note":"1,695 CZK."},{"name":"Olive-oil poached halibut","note":"Fish range 995-1,295 CZK."},{"name":"St Martin's goose menu","note":"Seasonal, November."}],"charter":{"price":"Around 2,000-3,000 CZK per head à la carte before wine; mains 995-1,695 CZK (own site, Sept 2026)","book":"1-2 weeks ahead for the terrace in season","dress":"Smart casual","warn":"You pay a view premium; no guide recognition this cycle","fit":"Charles Bridge from the waterline · Private room: Group bookings, catering and private boat excursions with captain; room size not published"},"web":"https://www.kampapark.com/","hot_this_month":"St Martin's goose menu is a house fixture for 11 November; check the site in late October."},
    {"id":"mlynec","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":17,"name":"Mlýnec","short":"Mlýnec","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Novotného lávka, the mill spur beside Charles Bridge","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ml%C3%BDnec+restaurant+Praha","badge":"RIVER","tags":["MICHELIN €€€ band; set menus (Sept 2026)","Online via mlynec.apetee.com; last lunch booking 13:30 weekdays.","Weekend brunch or sunset"],"productTags":["charles bridge","czech revival","balcony"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 11:30-15:00, 17:00-22:00; Sat-Sun 11:30-15:00, 17:30-22:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Mlýnec — the little mill — sits on Novotného lávka, the spur of old water-mill buildings that juts into the Vltava beside the bridge, with a balcony right over it. Vladimír Vaníček says he revives forgotten Czech specialities with modern technique. It is the Old Town bank's answer to Kampa Park, looking straight across the water at it.","address":"Novotného lávka 9, Praha 1","phone":"+420 277 000 777","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.08541,"lng":14.413595,"category":"river","subcat":"ON THE VLTAVA","hook":"A little mill on a spur in the river, with floor-to-ceiling windows on Charles Bridge.","person":"Vladimír Vaníček (chef)","signature":"The balcony table with Charles Bridge ahead","verdict":"The river-view dinner to pick if the guest also cares about the plate.","caveat":"Still bridge-adjacent pricing.","price_range":"MICHELIN €€€ band; set menus (Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online via mlynec.apetee.com; last lunch booking 13:30 weekdays.","best_time":"Weekend brunch or sunset","dishes":[{"name":"'The Most Popular' set menu","note":"The house greatest hits."},{"name":"Tartare & Steak menu","note":"The meat set."},{"name":"Vegetarian set menu","note":"Listed by MICHELIN."},{"name":"Weekend brunch","note":"With Aperol Spritz, per the site."}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Selected","full":"MICHELIN Selected, Guide Czechia 2025","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, Dec 2025"},"charter":{"price":"MICHELIN €€€ band; set menus, price on request (Sept 2026)","book":"1-2 weeks ahead online for window tables","dress":"Smart casual","warn":"Window tables are the whole point; confirm one in writing","fit":"Charles Bridge and the weir from floor-to-ceiling windows and a balcony · Private room: Private events and groups accepted; size on request"},"web":"https://www.mlynec.cz/"},
    {"id":"restaurace-vltava","cat":"shop","tier":"several","priority":18,"name":"Restaurace Vltava","short":"Vltava","neighborhood":"Nové Město · on the quay at Rašínovo nábřeží, between Palacký and Jirásek bridges","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Restaurace+Vltava+Ra%C5%A1%C3%ADnovo+n%C3%A1b%C5%99e%C5%BE%C3%AD+Praha","badge":"RIVER","tags":["Mains 269-349 CZK; desserts 125-155 CZK (own site, Sept 2026)","Walk in; call for the terrace on a Saturday.","Saturday after the Náplavka market"],"productTags":["fish","since 1945","quay"],"hours":"Daily 11:00-22:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"The Soukup family built this wooden house on the quay in 1945, and the brothers Jan and René have run it since 1990; it has outlived communism and the floods of 2002 and 2013. Eighty seats at river level, the castle downstream. Carp à la Rožmberk — named for the lords who dug the carp ponds — is 269 CZK.","address":"Rašínovo nábřeží 2084/1, Praha 2","phone":"+420 727 923 481","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.074075,"lng":14.413674,"category":"river","subcat":"ON THE VLTAVA","hook":"A wooden fish house at water level since 1945, same family, a quarter of the bridge prices.","person":"Jan and René Soukup","signature":"Carp à la Rožmberk","verdict":"The working river table: a quarter of the Charles Bridge price, same water.","caveat":"Simple cooking; do not expect finesse.","price_range":"Mains 269-349 CZK; desserts 125-155 CZK (own site, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk in; call for the terrace on a Saturday.","best_time":"Saturday after the Náplavka market","dishes":[{"name":"Carp à la Rožmberk","note":"269 CZK; named after the South Bohemian lords who built the carp ponds."},{"name":"Grilled salmon with herbs","note":"349 CZK."},{"name":"Roast beef in pepper sauce","note":"319 CZK."}],"web":"https://www.restauracevltava.cz/","hot_this_month":"The Náplavka farmers market runs on the same quay every Saturday in October 2026 (3, 10, 17, 24, 31)."},
    {"id":"lokal-dlouhaaa","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":20,"name":"Lokál Dlouhááá","short":"Lokál Dlouhá","neighborhood":"Staré Město · north of Old Town Square, on Dlouhá","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lok%C3%A1l+Dlouh%C3%A1%C3%A1%C3%A1+Praha","badge":"TANKOVNA","tags":["Svíčková 325 Kč, schnitzel 355 Kč, tatarák 365 Kč (menu seen 27 Sept 2026)","Recommended for evenings; online on own site","Late lunch, 14:00–17:00"],"productTags":["tank beer","svíčková","tatarák"],"hours":"Mon–Sat 11:00–24:00, Sun 11:00–22:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Ambiente opened it in 2009 as 'a traditional Czech pub for the 21st century', and it reset what a central Prague pub could be. About 1,300 people a day drink unpasteurised Pilsner Urquell drawn from tanks directly under the taps, poured as hladinka, šnyt or mlíko on request. The kitchen is plain Czech on purpose — svíčková, goulash, tartare mixed to order.","address":"Dlouhá 33, Praha 1","phone":"+420 734 283 874","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.090696,"lng":14.425758,"category":"czech","subcat":"THE CZECH KITCHEN","hook":"69.78 metres of beer hall, twelve tanks of Pilsner under the taps, and pub food made that day.","person":"Chef Petr Jelínek; manager Daniel Proksch","signature":"Beef tartare (365 Kč) with a mlíko first","verdict":"The benchmark for tank Pilsner and pub cooking in the centre; start here and judge everything else against it.","caveat":"It is on every list, so evenings are loud and full; the 1970s canteen décor is deliberate, not cosy.","price_range":"Svíčková 325 Kč, schnitzel 355 Kč, tatarák 365 Kč (menu seen 27 Sept 2026)","reservation":"Recommended for evenings; online on own site","best_time":"Late lunch, 14:00–17:00","dishes":[{"name":"Svíčková (braised beef with cranberry jam)","note":"325 Kč; the cream-vegetable sauce is the test of any Czech kitchen"},{"name":"Freshly mixed beef tartare","note":"365 Kč; mixed to order, with fried bread and garlic to rub"},{"name":"Fried edam with tartar sauce","note":"315 Kč; smažený sýr made with artisan cheese"},{"name":"Beef shin goulash","note":"305 Kč"},{"name":"Pickled knackwurst (utopenec)","note":"129 Kč; the drowned-man sausage, a beer snack"},{"name":"Tripe soup","note":"79 Kč"}],"charter":{"price":"Mains 209–495 CZK; svíčková 325 CZK (own menu, 4 Oct 2026)","book":"Online up to 12 on its own site; above 12 email dlouha@ambi.cz","dress":"Casual beer hall","warn":"Loud and full most evenings; open to midnight Mon–Sat, 22:00 Sun","fit":"The biggest room on this list: a 69.78-metre tank-pub hall"},"web":"https://lokal-dlouha.ambi.cz/en/","hot_this_month":"Daily board changes; on 28 Sept 2026 it listed bramborák with smoked meat and sauerkraut, 165 CZK."},
    {"id":"u-kroka","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":21,"name":"U Kroka","short":"U Kroka","neighborhood":"Vyšehrad · below the fortress walls","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Kroka+Praha","badge":"HOSPODA","tags":["Mid-range Czech pub prices; mains not published on site (checked Sept 2026)","Strongly recommended","Lunch after walking Vyšehrad"],"productTags":["svíčková","family","Vyšehrad"],"hours":"Daily 11:30–23:00, kitchen break 16:00–17:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Yvet, Tomáš and Bára run a small non-smoking room that takes its name and tradition from an inn opened on the Vyšehrad promenade in 1895. The kitchen cooks the Czech classics without flavour enhancers, and its svíčková is the one Praguers send friends to. The Infatuation puts it 'a step or two above typical Czech pub grub'.","address":"Vratislavova 28/12, Praha 2","phone":"+420 775 905 022","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.066583,"lng":14.417846,"category":"czech","subcat":"THE CZECH KITCHEN","hook":"A family pub under Vyšehrad, in an inn tradition that goes back to 1895.","person":"Yvet, Tomáš and Bára (family owners)","signature":"Svíčková na smetaně","verdict":"The best reason to climb Vyšehrad after the view: a proper sauce in a room with regulars.","caveat":"Small and popular; without a booking you will likely be turned away at dinner. Note the one-hour kitchen break.","price_range":"Mid-range Czech pub prices; mains not published on site (checked Sept 2026)","reservation":"Strongly recommended","best_time":"Lunch after walking Vyšehrad","dishes":[{"name":"Svíčková na smetaně","note":"the house reputation"},{"name":"Guláš","note":"beef goulash with dumplings"},{"name":"Roast duck","note":"with red cabbage and dumplings"},{"name":"Kulajda","note":"South Bohemian dill and mushroom soup with a poached egg"},{"name":"Garlic soup (česnečka)","note":""}],"web":"https://www.ukroka.cz/en","hot_this_month":"Daily 10:00–22:30; the Gothic garden beside the Franciscan garden before the cold sets in."},
    {"id":"u-mateje","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":22,"name":"U Matěje","short":"U Matěje","neighborhood":"Praha 6 · Hanspaulka villas, under chestnut trees","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Mat%C4%9Bje+Praha","badge":"BIB","tags":["MICHELIN €€ (checked Sept 2026)","Online, email rezervace@umateje1.cz, or phone","Weekend lunch in the garden"],"productTags":["goose","carp","Bib Gourmand"],"hours":"Daily 11:30–23:00 (own site and MICHELIN, Sept 2026)","why":"Jan Punčochář, one of the country's best-known chefs, opened it in 2019: 'Having a restaurant focused on honest Czech cuisine was always my dream.' MICHELIN names carp fries with dill mayonnaise, stuffed goose stomach and heart, and pulled goose with sauerkraut and potato pancakes — the old Bohemian kitchen, offal included, with fine-dining discipline, under tall chestnuts.","address":"U Matěje 152/1, Praha 6","phone":"+420 602 154 865","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.113562,"lng":14.379048,"category":"czech","subcat":"THE CZECH KITCHEN","hook":"A famous chef's roadside-inn dream in Prague 6: goose, offal and carp fries, at pub prices.","person":"Jan Punčochář (chef-founder)","signature":"Pulled goose with sauerkraut and bramboráky","verdict":"The most serious Czech cooking at pub prices in the city, worth the tram ride out.","caveat":"A long way from the centre (tram to Hanspaulka, then a walk); book the garden in advance on warm days.","price_range":"MICHELIN €€ (checked Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online, email rezervace@umateje1.cz, or phone","best_time":"Weekend lunch in the garden","dishes":[{"name":"Carp fries with dill mayonnaise","note":"Czech Christmas fish turned into a bar snack"},{"name":"Stuffed goose stomach and heart","note":"offal from the old repertoire"},{"name":"Pulled goose with sauerkraut and potato pancakes","note":"the house's version of the Sunday roast"},{"name":"Svíčková","note":"a year-round staple"}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Bib 2026","full":"Bib Gourmand, MICHELIN Guide Czechia","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, current listing (checked 27 Sept 2026); Gault&Millau two toques per own site"},"web":"https://www.umateje1.cz/"},
    {"id":"sapa-market","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":24,"name":"SAPA (TTTM Sapa)","short":"SAPA","neighborhood":"Praha 4-Libuš · the southern edge, bus from Kačerov","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=SAPA+Praha+Libu%C5%A1","badge":"MARKET","tags":["Bowls roughly 150–250 Kč (unverified range; no printed prices found, Sept 2026)","None","Weekend late morning"],"productTags":["Vietnamese","market","cash"],"hours":"Market roughly 8:00–22:00; stalls vary (Food on the Move guide, updated 6 Sept 2026)","why":"Around 2000 a closed meat-packing plant in Libuš became SAPA, now the largest Vietnamese market in Central Europe: wholesale halls, grocers, lawyers, a kindergarten, a Buddhist temple and dozens of kitchens. Bún chả is grilled over charcoal outside, bánh cuốn steamed to order upstairs, and a Hải Phòng fish soup is made with Czech carp. Sources disagree on the opening year.","address":"Libušská 319/126, Praha 4-Libuš","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.003201,"lng":14.47286,"category":"vietnamese","subcat":"LITTLE HANOI","hook":"Prague's Little Hanoi: a Vietnamese town of halls, temple and kitchens on an old poultry plant.","signature":"A lap of the food halls: bún chả, bánh cuốn, carp soup","verdict":"The single most un-Paris thing to eat in Prague, and the best half-day food trip in the city.","caveat":"Bring cash; signage is mostly Vietnamese; the wholesale halls are not pretty and are not meant to be.","price_range":"Bowls roughly 150–250 Kč (unverified range; no printed prices found, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Weekend late morning","dishes":[{"name":"Bún chả at Hải Hà","note":"see its own card"},{"name":"Bánh cuốn at Phương Phượng","note":"upper floor; one portion feeds two"},{"name":"Duck at Dũng Liên","note":"grilled duck with broth, noodles and herbs"},{"name":"Crab soup at Sành Quán","note":""},{"name":"Chè at Chè Sài Gòn","note":"sweet bean and jelly desserts"},{"name":"Bún cá Hải Phòng — with Czech carp","note":"Hải Phòng's bún cá is a fish broth with dill and fried fish; in Bohemia the fish is carp, the pond fish Czechs buy live from barrels before Christmas. So the one dish at SAPA that uses the most Czech ingredient of all is a northern Vietnamese soup,"}]},
    {"id":"hai-ha-sapa","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":25,"name":"Hải Hà","short":"Hải Hà","neighborhood":"SAPA, Libuš · follow the charcoal smoke","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hai+Ha+SAPA+Praha","badge":"BUN CHA","tags":["Not published (Sept 2026)","None","Lunch"],"productTags":["bún chả","charcoal","cash"],"hours":"Within SAPA market hours; not published","why":"Bún chả is Hanoi's lunch: grilled pork belly and patties in a warm sweet-sour broth, cold rice noodles and a heap of herbs. Hải Hà grills it outside on charcoal, Czech food writers single it out again and again, and it hangs a 'Best Bún Chả in Prague' certificate on the wall. Pork belly is the meat Czechs understand best; this is Vietnam's answer to it.","address":"","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.003512,"lng":14.473471,"category":"vietnamese","subcat":"LITTLE HANOI","hook":"Pork belly over charcoal at SAPA's door: Hanoi's lunch, done the Hanoi way.","signature":"Bún chả","verdict":"If you eat one thing at SAPA, make it this.","caveat":"Cash, crowds at lunch, no English menu guaranteed.","price_range":"Not published (Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Bún chả","note":"grilled pork belly and patties, broth, noodles, herbs"},{"name":"Nem rán","note":"fried spring rolls, often added to bún chả in Hanoi"}]},
    {"id":"pho-vietnam-anglicka","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":26,"name":"Pho Vietnam Tuan & Lan","short":"Pho Vietnam Anglická","neighborhood":"Vinohrady · a cellar a few minutes from Náměstí Míru","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pho+Vietnam+Tuan+Lan+Anglick%C3%A1+Praha","badge":"PHO","tags":["Budget; bowls priced for a weekday lunch (exact prices not seen, Sept 2026)","Walk-in","Weekday lunch before 12:00"],"productTags":["phở","cellar","Hanoi"],"hours":"Daily 11:00–22:00 (listings, 2026)","why":"The Infatuation picks this basement as the Vietnamese room among its twenty best in Prague. The broth leans Hanoi rather than Saigon — clearer, with star anise and ginger, fewer sweet sauces — and northern dishes like bún chả and bánh cuốn sit beside it. It is how most Praguers meet Vietnamese food: a big, cheap bowl at lunch.","address":"Anglická 529/15, Praha 2","phone":"+420 606 707 880","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.078448,"lng":14.448266,"category":"vietnamese","subcat":"LITTLE HANOI","hook":"A basement phở room with a Hanoi-clear broth, between Náměstí Míru and the offices.","person":"Tuan and Lan (owners, per the name)","signature":"Phở bò","verdict":"The one central phở worth the detour when SAPA is too far.","caveat":"A cellar that gets very warm; service is quick, not chatty.","price_range":"Budget; bowls priced for a weekday lunch (exact prices not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk-in","best_time":"Weekday lunch before 12:00","dishes":[{"name":"Phở bò","note":"beef phở, star anise and ginger"},{"name":"Bún chả","note":"northern speciality"},{"name":"Bánh cuốn","note":"steamed rice rolls"}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Infatuation 20 Best","full":"The 20 Best Restaurants in Prague","cosign":"The Infatuation, 2025"}},
    {"id":"turkestan","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":28,"name":"Turkestan Restaurace","short":"Turkestan","neighborhood":"Žižkov · Bořivojova, among the old tenement pubs","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Turkestan+Restaurace+Praha","badge":"PLOV","tags":["Budget (menu prices not seen, Sept 2026)","Walk-in","Lunch"],"productTags":["Uzbek","halal","no alcohol"],"hours":"Not published on a current source; check before going","why":"Žižkov claims more pubs per head than anywhere in Prague, which is exactly why this halal room is useful: it serves no alcohol. Most diners are from Uzbekistan or Kazakhstan. The Infatuation sends you for hand-pulled noodle soup with lamb and plates of plov 'when you need to give your gastrointestinal system a time out from beer and sausages'.","address":"Bořivojova 883/116, Praha 3","phone":"+420 608 835 033","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.082259,"lng":14.445198,"category":"ethnic","subcat":"THE OTHER KITCHENS","hook":"Lagman and plov in Žižkov, the pub district — and no alcohol licence at all.","signature":"Lagman, then plov","verdict":"The best reset meal in a beer city.","caveat":"Little English or Czech spoken; opening hours not reliably published.","price_range":"Budget (menu prices not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk-in","best_time":"Lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Lagman","note":"hand-pulled noodle soup with lamb and carrots; also fried"},{"name":"Plov","note":"rice with beef, carrots and crisp bits"},{"name":"Ayran","note":"house-made salted yoghurt drink"}],"signal_chip":{"label":"Infatuation 20 Best","full":"The 20 Best Restaurants in Prague","cosign":"The Infatuation, Nov 2025"}},
    {"id":"polevkarna-pani-manco","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":29,"name":"Polévkárna paní Mančo","short":"Paní Mančo","neighborhood":"Vinohrady · Bělehradská, a weekday soup counter","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pol%C3%A9vk%C3%A1rna+pan%C3%AD+Man%C4%8Do+Praha","badge":"SOUP","tags":["Borscht 130 Kč, khinkali (5) 290 Kč, adjaruli 330 Kč (own site, seen Sept 2026)","Walk-in","Weekday lunch"],"productTags":["Georgian","soup","weekday"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 10:00–20:00 per own site; another listing says 7:30–22:00. Closed weekends (Sept 2026)","why":"Manana Toidze opened her soup room in 2013 and cooks half Czech weekday lunch, half Georgian home food, with vegetables from Czech farmers. Georgian beef borscht is 130 Kč for 400 ml; five khinkali are 290 Kč — hold them by the knot and drink the broth first. Prices you would pay for a coffee on the square.","address":"Bělehradská 643/77, Praha 2","phone":"+420 776 749 953","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.073555,"lng":14.432883,"category":"ethnic","subcat":"THE OTHER KITCHENS","hook":"A woman from Tbilisi has fed Vinohrady soup and khinkali since 2013.","person":"Manana Toidze (owner-cook)","signature":"Georgian beef borscht and khinkali","verdict":"The most personal lunch counter in Vinohrady.","caveat":"Weekdays only; hours disagree between sources, so arrive at lunch.","price_range":"Borscht 130 Kč, khinkali (5) 290 Kč, adjaruli 330 Kč (own site, seen Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk-in","best_time":"Weekday lunch","dishes":[{"name":"Gruzínský boršč","note":"Georgian beef borscht, 400 ml, 130 Kč"},{"name":"Chinkali s masem","note":"five meat dumplings, 290 Kč; hold by the knot, drink the broth first"},{"name":"Chačapuri se sýrem","note":"small cheese bread, 155 Kč"},{"name":"Adžaruli chačapuri","note":"boat-shaped, 330 Kč"},{"name":"Harira","note":"Moroccan chickpea soup, one of the rotating soups"}],"web":"https://www.polevkarna-soup.com/"},
    {"id":"dhaba-beas","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":31,"name":"Dhaba Beas","short":"Dhaba Beas","neighborhood":"All over Prague · central branch on Na Poříčí","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dhaba+Beas+Na+Po%C5%99%C3%AD%C4%8D%C3%AD+Praha","badge":"BY WEIGHT","tags":["By weight; current price per 100 g posted in branch (Sept 2026)","None","Before 12:00 or after 13:30"],"productTags":["vegetarian","Indian","cheap"],"hours":"Branch-dependent; see own site map (Sept 2026)","why":"Prague's most successful Indian kitchen is a canteen: dal, sabzi, rice and chapati, largely vegan, weighed at the till by the 100 grams. The founders came back from India with an Indian cook and opened one small buffet more than fifteen years ago; there are now 27. Students and office workers eat here for the price of a beer and a half.","address":"Na Poříčí 26, Praha 1 (one of many branches)","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.073374,"lng":14.433372,"category":"ethnic","subcat":"THE OTHER KITCHENS","hook":"Dal, sabzi and chapati by weight: the Indian canteen that grew from one room to 27.","signature":"A plate of dal, sabzi, rice and chapati","verdict":"The cheapest good vegetables in Prague, and a fair picture of how the city eats at noon.","caveat":"Self-service and functional; the flavour is gentle Indian, tuned to Czech palates.","price_range":"By weight; current price per 100 g posted in branch (Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Before 12:00 or after 13:30","dishes":[{"name":"Dal","note":""},{"name":"Vegetable sabzi of the day","note":""},{"name":"Chapati","note":""},{"name":"Lassi","note":""}],"web":"https://dhababeas.cz/en/about-us"},
    {"id":"cafe-savoy","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":32,"name":"Café Savoy","short":"Savoy","neighborhood":"Malá Strana / Újezd · at the Legion Bridge end of Vítězná","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caf%C3%A9+Savoy+Praha","badge":"CAFÉ","tags":["Grand-café prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","Required at weekends","8:00 weekdays"],"productTags":["breakfast","grand café","pastry"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 8:00–22:00, Sat–Sun 9:00–22:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Savoy opened in 1893 on the corner of Vítězná, one bridge from the National Theatre, and its painted ceiling is from that year. By day it is a Viennese café; at night Tomáš Vlček cooks a quieter, French-leaning menu. The pastries are baked with Myšák, the confectioner founded in 1911, so its morning cabinet is the surest taste of Prague's old cakes.","address":"Vítězná 5, Praha 5","phone":"+420 731 136 144","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.080926,"lng":14.407216,"category":"breakfast","subcat":"SNÍDANĚ","hook":"Breakfast under an 1893 ceiling, with a cake cabinet baked by a confectioner of 1911.","person":"Chef Tomáš Vlček","signature":"Breakfast plate and a Savoy cake slice","verdict":"The grand-café breakfast to choose over the Old Town ones.","caveat":"Reservations needed at weekends; a tourist favourite, priced like one.","price_range":"Grand-café prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Required at weekends","best_time":"8:00 weekdays","dishes":[{"name":"Viennese coffee","note":""},{"name":"Pastry from the cabinet (with Myšák)","note":""},{"name":"Savoy cake","note":"the house cake"}],"web":"https://cafesavoy.ambi.cz/en/"},
    {"id":"eska-karlin","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":33,"name":"Eska Karlín","short":"Eska","neighborhood":"Karlín · in a converted factory on Pernerova","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Eska+Karl%C3%ADn+Praha","badge":"PEKÁRNA","tags":["Mid-range (menu prices not seen, Sept 2026)","None for the bakery","Weekday 8:00"],"productTags":["sourdough","breakfast","Karlín"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 8:00–18:00, Sat–Sun 9:00–18:00; breakfast served late (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Ambiente's bakery fills the ground floor of a Karlín factory hall, with a shop and a breakfast room run around head baker Jaroslav Kozdělka. The sourdough loaves are named for their rye ratio — 33 every day, 66 on Fridays — beside buchty and koláče, the Czech yeast pastries. A second Eska at Letná is bakery and coffee only.","address":"Pernerova 49, Praha 8","phone":"+420 731 140 884","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.091362,"lng":14.454374,"category":"breakfast","subcat":"SNÍDANĚ","hook":"A factory-hall bakery that names its loaves by number: bread 33 daily, bread 66 on Fridays.","person":"Head baker Jaroslav Kozdělka; manager David Marek","signature":"Breakfast with bread 33, then a koláč","verdict":"The best bread-first breakfast in Prague; take a loaf back to the galley.","caveat":"No reservations for the bakery; weekend queues from opening.","price_range":"Mid-range (menu prices not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None for the bakery","best_time":"Weekday 8:00","dishes":[{"name":"Bread 33","note":"the house sourdough"},{"name":"Bread 66","note":"Fridays only"},{"name":"Koláč / buchta","note":"Czech yeasted pastries"}],"web":"https://eska.karlin.ambi.cz/en"},
    {"id":"bockem","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":34,"name":"Bockem","short":"Bockem","neighborhood":"Smíchov · a 26-seat room in an early-20th-century house","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bockem+Praha","badge":"BRUNCH","tags":["Upper mid-range (not seen, Sept 2026)","Online via bockem.apetee.com","Saturday 9:00"],"productTags":["brunch","Smíchov","small room"],"hours":"Mornings Thu–Fri 8:00–13:00, Sat–Sun 9:00–14:00; dinner Wed–Sat 18:00–23:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Ondřej Kynčl's small room is a MICHELIN-selected dinner restaurant that also opens for breakfast, including a 'Morning Degustation'. The Infatuation sends you for the croque monsieur and the high-rise benedict soufflé. It is the rare Prague breakfast cooked by a serious kitchen, in an early-20th-century house few visitors find. Book it for a slow morning.","address":"Elišky Peškové 1095/5, Praha 5","phone":"+420 770 101 223","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.077292,"lng":14.40519,"category":"breakfast","subcat":"SNÍDANĚ","hook":"Twenty-six seats where a dinner kitchen cooks breakfast: a benedict soufflé and a morning tasting.","person":"Chef Ondřej Kynčl","signature":"Benedict soufflé","verdict":"The ambitious breakfast; book it for the one morning you want to sit for two hours.","caveat":"No breakfast Mon–Wed; small room, book ahead.","price_range":"Upper mid-range (not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online via bockem.apetee.com","best_time":"Saturday 9:00","dishes":[{"name":"Croque monsieur","note":""},{"name":"Benedict soufflé","note":"the house trick"},{"name":"Morning Degustation","note":"a breakfast tasting menu"}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN 2025","full":"MICHELIN Selected (per own site)","cosign":"Own site; The Infatuation Nov 2025"},"web":"https://bockem.cz/en/"},
    {"id":"kantyna","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":35,"name":"Kantýna","short":"Kantýna","neighborhood":"Nové Město · a former bank off Wenceslas Square","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kant%C3%BDna+Praha","badge":"BUTCHER","tags":["Steak priced by weight at the counter (prices not published online, Sept 2026)","None taken","15:00–18:00"],"productTags":["dry-aged","open fire","no bookings"],"hours":"Mon–Sat 11:30–23:00, Sun 11:30–22:00; food until 22:00 (Sun 21:00) (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Ambiente built this canteen inside a former bank: a counter of dry-aged Czech beef and pork, an open fire, and a marble table for twenty or thirty strangers. You choose from the counter, Jan Macík's butchers cut it, Jakub Hlávka's grill cooks it. Start with bone marrow; The Infatuation calls the burger the best in Prague.","address":"Politických vězňů 1511/5, Praha 1","phone":"+420 605 593 328","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.083384,"lng":14.428757,"category":"grills","subcat":"THE FIRE","hook":"A butcher's counter and an open fire in an old bank hall: point at the cut, they grill it.","person":"Chef Jakub Hlávka; chief butcher Jan Macík","signature":"Dry-aged steak from the counter, bone marrow first","verdict":"The best-run meat room in the centre and the easiest solo meal in town.","caveat":"No reservations; peak hours mean queuing and standing.","price_range":"Steak priced by weight at the counter (prices not published online, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None taken","best_time":"15:00–18:00","dishes":[{"name":"Dry-aged steak","note":"from the counter, by weight"},{"name":"Bone marrow","note":""},{"name":"Burger","note":"The Infatuation's best in Prague"},{"name":"Pastrami","note":""},{"name":"Pig heart","note":""}],"charter":{"price":"Steak priced by weight at the counter (not published online)","book":"None taken: walk in and queue","dress":"Casual, counter service","warn":"Food orders until 22:00 Mon–Sat, 21:00 Sun","fit":"The one true walk-in: a butcher's counter and an open fire in a former bank"},"web":"https://www.kantyna.ambi.cz/en/"},
    {"id":"nase-maso","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":36,"name":"Naše maso","short":"Naše maso","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Gurmet Pasáž on Dlouhá","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Na%C5%A1e+maso+Dlouh%C3%A1+Praha","badge":"BUTCHER","tags":["Budget to mid (counter prices not published, Sept 2026)","None","11:00 opening"],"productTags":["Přeštice pig","counter","sekaná"],"hours":"Mon–Thu 11:00–22:00, Fri–Sat 10:00–22:00, Sun closed (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Naše maso is a butcher first: Czech beef, pork from the Přeštice Black Pied, a heritage Bohemian breed, and smoked meats made to old recipes. The counter cooks the butcher's canon — burger, sekaná meatloaf in a bun, steak tartare, sausages — and you eat it standing at the counter or on the pavement.","address":"Dlouhá 727/39, Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.090798,"lng":14.426856,"category":"grills","subcat":"THE FIRE","hook":"A working butcher on Dlouhá that cooks its own meatloaf in a bun at the counter.","signature":"Sekaná in a roll","verdict":"The fastest serious meat lunch in Prague, three doors from Lokál.","caveat":"Tiny, standing room only; closed Sundays.","price_range":"Budget to mid (counter prices not published, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"11:00 opening","dishes":[{"name":"Sekaná v housce","note":"meatloaf in a bun"},{"name":"Burger","note":""},{"name":"Steak tartare","note":""},{"name":"House sausages","note":""}],"web":"https://nasemaso.ambi.cz/en/"},
    {"id":"vycep-korunni","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":37,"name":"Výčep","short":"Výčep","neighborhood":"Vinohrady · far end of Korunní","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=V%C3%BD%C4%8Dep+Korunn%C3%AD+Praha","badge":"BIB","tags":["MICHELIN €€€ (checked Sept 2026)","Direct; recommended","Weekday lunch menu"],"productTags":["smokehouse","Moravian","Bib Gourmand"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 11:00–23:00, Sat 12:00–23:00, Sun 12:00–22:00 (own site and MICHELIN, Sept 2026)","why":"Výčep calls itself a modern pub from Wallachia, the Moravian-Carpathian hill country, and makes its own bread, cheese, cured and smoked meat, fermented vegetables, kombucha and spirits, with Dalešice beer on tap. MICHELIN picks out langoš with sheep's cheese and house-smoked cracklings, and a větrník for dessert. The Infatuation sends you for the short rib and the fire-grilled trout.","address":"Korunní 1304/92, Praha 10","phone":"+420 720 120 100","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.075258,"lng":14.453626,"category":"grills","subcat":"THE FIRE","hook":"A modern Wallachian pub in Vinohrady that smokes, cures, ferments and distils everything itself.","person":"Kolektiv group","signature":"Langoš with sheep's cheese and smoked cracklings","verdict":"The fire and the smokehouse of Moravia, in Vinohrady, at a Bib price.","caveat":"Loud and crowded; it is a long walk out along Korunní.","price_range":"MICHELIN €€€ (checked Sept 2026)","reservation":"Direct; recommended","best_time":"Weekday lunch menu","dishes":[{"name":"Langoš with sheep's cheese and house-smoked cracklings","note":""},{"name":"Short rib","note":""},{"name":"Fire-grilled rainbow trout","note":""},{"name":"Větrník","note":"choux with caramel and vanilla cream"}],"signal_chip":{"label":"MICHELIN Bib 2026","full":"Bib Gourmand, MICHELIN Guide Czechia","cosign":"MICHELIN Guide, current listing (checked 27 Sept 2026)"},"web":"https://www.vycepkorunni.cz/"},
    {"id":"havelska-koruna","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":38,"name":"Havelská Koruna","short":"Havelská Koruna","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Havelská, by the market street","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Havelsk%C3%A1+Koruna+Praha","badge":"JÍDELNA","tags":["Svíčková 189 Kč, goulash 179 Kč, schnitzel 188 Kč (own site, Sept 2026)","None","11:30"],"productTags":["canteen","cheap","Old Town"],"hours":"Daily; exact hours not published on own site (delivery 10:00–20:00, Sept 2026)","why":"The most central jídelna left: you take a ticket at the door, choose from at least forty dishes, the cooks mark the ticket, and you pay on the way out. Svíčková is 189 Kč, goulash 179, with Pilsner on tap — a hundred metres from the market stalls selling trdelník to tourists.","address":"Havelská 23, Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.085525,"lng":14.421665,"category":"fast-food","subcat":"THE FAST PLATE","hook":"A paper ticket at the door, forty Czech dishes at the counter, everything under 200 Kč.","signature":"Svíčková, 189 Kč","verdict":"The honest-price Czech plate in the Old Town.","caveat":"Canteen lighting and trays; do not lose the ticket.","price_range":"Svíčková 189 Kč, goulash 179 Kč, schnitzel 188 Kč (own site, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"11:30","dishes":[{"name":"Svíčková na smetaně","note":"189 Kč"},{"name":"Beef goulash","note":"179 Kč"},{"name":"Dill sauce with beef (koprovka)","note":"181 Kč"},{"name":"Chicken schnitzel","note":"188 Kč"}],"web":"https://www.havelska-koruna.cz/"},
    {"id":"jidelna-svetozor","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":39,"name":"Jídelna Světozor","short":"Světozor","neighborhood":"Nové Město · inside the Světozor passage off Wenceslas Square","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=J%C3%ADdelna+Sv%C4%9Btozor+Praha","badge":"JÍDELNA","tags":["Menu 169 Kč, duck 219 Kč (Meníčka.cz, 27 Sept 2026)","None","11:00–12:00"],"productTags":["canteen","lunch","169 Kč"],"hours":"Daily 10:00–15:00 (Meníčka.cz, 27 Sept 2026)","why":"A lunch canteen in the Světozor passage off Wenceslas Square, with more than twenty dishes a day and a set of soup, main and dessert for 169 Kč, 120 for seniors. On 27 September 2026 that meant beef broth with noodles and a roast duck quarter with red cabbage. Some sources say it dates to 1912 as the first self-service in the country; we could not verify it.","address":"Vodičkova 39, pasáž Světozor, Praha 1","phone":"+420 721 594 723","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.081723,"lng":14.425078,"category":"fast-food","subcat":"THE FAST PLATE","hook":"Soup, a main and dessert for 169 Kč, in a canteen inside the Světozor arcade.","signature":"The daily three-course menu","verdict":"Lunch as pensioners and office workers eat it, steps from the square.","caveat":"Lunch only; no evening service.","price_range":"Menu 169 Kč, duck 219 Kč (Meníčka.cz, 27 Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"11:00–12:00","dishes":[{"name":"Daily menu (soup, main, dessert)","note":"169 Kč"},{"name":"Roast duck quarter, red cabbage","note":"219 Kč"},{"name":"Smažený sýr","note":"fried cheese"},{"name":"Segedínský guláš","note":"pork and sauerkraut goulash"}],"web":"https://jidelnasvetozor.webnode.cz/"},
    {"id":"centraal","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":40,"name":"Centraal","short":"Centraal","neighborhood":"Nové Město · on the Rašínovo embankment","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Centraal+Ra%C5%A1%C3%ADnovo+n%C3%A1b%C5%99e%C5%BE%C3%AD+Praha","badge":"CHICKEN","tags":["Not published (Sept 2026)","None","Opening, 12:00"],"productTags":["fried chicken","takeaway","river"],"hours":"Tue–Sun 12:00–22:00, closes when sold out (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Taste of Prague named it among the openings of 2025 for the best fried-chicken sandwich in town, served with a glass of something sparkling. The house line is 'seasoning is a skill, not routine'. It sits on Rašínovo nábřeží, which makes that stretch of the river one of the better short food walks in the city.","address":"Rašínovo nábřeží 388/48, Praha 2","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.070253,"lng":14.414654,"category":"fast-food","subcat":"THE FAST PLATE","hook":"Hot chicken sandwiches and sparkling wine on the embankment, until the chicken runs out.","signature":"Hot chicken sandwich","verdict":"The one fast plate in Prague worth planning around.","caveat":"Closed Mondays; sells out.","price_range":"Not published (Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Opening, 12:00","dishes":[{"name":"Hot chicken sandwich","note":""},{"name":"Sparkling wine by the glass","note":""}],"web":"https://www.centraal.cz/"},
    {"id":"u-fleku","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":41,"name":"U Fleků","short":"U Fleků","neighborhood":"Nové Město · Křemencova, near the National Theatre","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Flek%C5%AF+Praha","badge":"1499","tags":["Tourist pricing; check the menu before ordering (Sept 2026)","Online form","Weekday afternoon in the courtyard"],"productTags":["brewpub","dark lager","history"],"hours":"Daily; hours on own site (checked Sept 2026)","why":"U Fleků has brewed on this spot since at least 1499 and took its name in 1762, when Jakub Flekovský bought it. Its dark lager is sold nowhere else, to some 1,200 seats in eight halls and a garden. A plaque records that Croatian students founded the football club Hajduk Split here in 1911. Expect accordions, and shots put on the table uninvited.","address":"Křemencova 11, Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.078744,"lng":14.417018,"category":"story","subcat":"THE OLD HOUSES","hook":"A brewery pub since 1499, pouring a dark 13° lager brewed on the spot and nowhere else.","signature":"Flekovský tmavý ležák 13°","verdict":"Go once for the beer and the history, refuse the shots, and eat elsewhere.","caveat":"Tourist pricing and unrequested shots appear on the bill; say no clearly.","price_range":"Tourist pricing; check the menu before ordering (Sept 2026)","reservation":"Online form","best_time":"Weekday afternoon in the courtyard","dishes":[{"name":"Flekovský 13° dark lager","note":"brewed on site, only here"},{"name":"Roast pork with dumplings","note":"the pub canon"}],"web":"https://www.ufleku.cz/en/"},
    {"id":"u-pinkasu","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":43,"name":"U Pinkasů","short":"U Pinkasů","neighborhood":"Nové Město · Jungmannovo náměstí, beside the Franciscan garden","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Pinkas%C5%AF+Praha","badge":"1843","tags":["Central pub prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","Phone or email","Afternoon in the garden"],"productTags":["Pilsner","history","garden"],"hours":"Daily 10:00–22:30 (Prague City Tourism, checked Sept 2026)","why":"Jakub Pinkas was a tailor who tasted the new Plzeň lager in April 1843 and opened a pub on it; Prague City Tourism records it as the first in the city to pour Pilsner on draught. The old pipe it first ran through is kept in the cellar. Palacký and Rieger had their own tables, and the garden backs onto the Gothic wall of the Franciscan grounds.","address":"Jungmannovo náměstí 16, Praha 1","phone":"+420 221 111 152","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.083205,"lng":14.423408,"category":"story","subcat":"THE OLD HOUSES","hook":"The first Pilsner on draught in Prague was poured here in 1843 — the pipe is in the cellar.","person":"Founded by Jakub Pinkas","signature":"Pilsner Urquell in the Gothic garden","verdict":"The pint with the best claim to history in Prague.","caveat":"The food is standard Czech pub; the point is the beer and the place.","price_range":"Dishes 299–699 CZK on the permanent menu (own site, seen 4 Oct 2026)","reservation":"Phone or email","best_time":"Afternoon in the garden","dishes":[{"name":"Pilsner Urquell","note":"since 1843"},{"name":"Velkopopovický Kozel dark","note":""}],"charter":{"price":"Dishes 299–699 CZK on the permanent menu (seen 4 Oct 2026)","book":"Phone or email","dress":"Casual pub","warn":"Open daily to 22:30; the food is standard pub, the point is the beer and the place","fit":"Since 1843, the first Pilsner on draught in Prague"},"web":"http://www.upinkasu.cz/"},
    {"id":"u-zlateho-tygra","cat":"berth","tier":"berth_top","priority":2,"name":"U Zlatého tygra","short":"Zlatý tygr","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Husova, between Charles Street and Old Town Square","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Zlat%C3%A9ho+tygra+Praha","badge":"HRABAL","tags":["Pub prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","Phone","15:00 opening"],"productTags":["Hrabal","Pilsner","history"],"hours":"Daily 15:00–23:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"The house is first mentioned in 1360; František Skořepa hung the walking tiger in 1935. Bohumil Hrabal drank here almost daily in the 1980s and 1990s, and on 11 January 1994 Václav Havel brought Bill Clinton and Madeleine Albright to meet him. Clinton had three beers and a schnitzel. Tables belong to regulars on set days, so newcomers mostly stand.","address":"Husova 17, Praha 1","phone":"+420 222 221 111","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.08579,"lng":14.417908,"category":"story","subcat":"THE OLD HOUSES","hook":"Hrabal's pub: Havel brought Clinton here on 11 January 1994, and he had three beers.","person":"Run by Jan Hendrych since 2014","signature":"Pilsner Urquell and a plate of cheese or pork","verdict":"The most storied pint in Prague, in a room that has not been redecorated for visitors.","caveat":"Regulars hold the tables; arrive at 15:00 opening to have a chance.","price_range":"Pub prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Phone","best_time":"15:00 opening","dishes":[{"name":"Pilsner Urquell","note":"the only beer"},{"name":"Pork neck with bread and mustard","note":"the house anecdote dish"}],"web":"https://www.uzlatehotygra.cz/en/"},
    {"id":"letna-beer-garden","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":44,"name":"Letenský zámeček and the Letná beer garden","short":"Letná garden","neighborhood":"Letná · the park plateau above the Vltava","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Letensk%C3%BD+z%C3%A1me%C4%8Dek+Praha","badge":"GARDEN","tags":["Garden prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","None in the garden","Late afternoon to sunset"],"productTags":["view","beer garden","seasonal"],"hours":"Restaurant year-round; beer-garden season dates not published (checked Sept 2026)","why":"The house beside it claims more than 150 years of tradition, and its garden is Prague's best-known: long tables under the trees, lager in plastic cups, and the bends of the river and its bridges laid out beneath you. A short walk away are the 1891 Hanavský pavilion and one of Europe's oldest carousels, from 1892.","address":"Letenské sady 341, Praha 7","phone":"+420 233 378 200","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.096349,"lng":14.425548,"category":"gardens","subcat":"GARDENS AND HILLS","hook":"Long tables under chestnuts, plastic cups, and every bridge of the city lined up below.","signature":"A plastic cup of lager at the edge, facing the river","verdict":"The one beer garden to see, on any dry afternoon.","caveat":"The outdoor bar is seasonal and weather-bound; by late October it may be closed.","price_range":"Garden prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None in the garden","best_time":"Late afternoon to sunset","dishes":[{"name":"Lager in a cup","note":""},{"name":"Klobása from the grill","note":"when the stand is running"}],"web":"https://www.letenskyzamecek.cz/","hot_this_month":"Early October: garden may still run on dry afternoons; season end not published."},
    {"id":"parukarka","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":45,"name":"Parukářka","short":"Parukářka","neighborhood":"Žižkov · the hill of Svatý Kříž, above the TV tower streets","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Paruk%C3%A1%C5%99ka+Praha","badge":"HILL","tags":["Pub prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","None","Sunset"],"productTags":["grill","view","Žižkov"],"hours":"Pub daily 14:00–24:00; outdoor stand Zastávka approx. early April–late October, 13:00–23:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"A small pub dug into the hill of Svatý Kříž, with a seasonal stand on top, playgrounds and a view over Žižkov's roofs. Guests may grill their own sausages. Beneath the same hill is Bunkr Bezovka, a Cold War shelter turned music club with a climbing wall. Locals, dogs and bags of klobásy; no tourists, by design.","address":"","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.085192,"lng":14.460678,"category":"gardens","subcat":"GARDENS AND HILLS","hook":"A pub cut into a hill above Žižkov, with a grill you can use and a Cold War bunker below.","signature":"Your own klobása on their grill, a beer from the stand","verdict":"The most local open-air beer in Prague.","caveat":"Closing times are approximate; the outdoor stand ends late October.","price_range":"Pub prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Sunset","dishes":[{"name":"Draught beer","note":""},{"name":"Bring-your-own grill","note":""}],"web":"https://www.parukarka.cz/","hot_this_month":"Outdoor stand runs until roughly late October 2026."},
    {"id":"zlute-lazne","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":46,"name":"Žluté lázně","short":"Žluté lázně","neighborhood":"Podolí · on the right bank upstream of Vyšehrad","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C5%BDlut%C3%A9+l%C3%A1zn%C4%9B+Praha","badge":"RIVER","tags":["Not published (Sept 2026)","None","Warm afternoon"],"productTags":["river","summer","beach bar"],"hours":"Season opened 1 May 2026; closing date not published (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Prague's historic river bathing ground at Podolí is now a summer complex of sport, a beach bar and twelve places to eat, from grills to Neapolitan pizza and gelato. It is where the city goes to sit beside its river rather than photograph it. The 2026 season opened on 1 May; the site does not say when it closes.","address":"","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.047772,"lng":14.413397,"category":"gardens","subcat":"GARDENS AND HILLS","hook":"The old river baths at Podolí, where the Vltava is a place to sit rather than look at.","signature":"A beer on the sand by the river","verdict":"A summer place; in October check before you go.","caveat":"Seasonal; ticketed entry at times; season end not published.","price_range":"Not published (Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Warm afternoon","dishes":[{"name":"Grill","note":""},{"name":"Neapolitan pizza","note":""},{"name":"Gelato","note":""}],"web":"https://www.zlutelazne.cz/","hot_this_month":"Season end not published; likely winding down in October."},
    {"id":"sisters-bistro","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":47,"name":"Sisters","short":"Sisters","neighborhood":"Staré Město · Dlouhá","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sisters+bistro+Dlouh%C3%A1+Praha","badge":"CHLEBÍČEK","tags":["53–65 Kč per chlebíček (own site, Sept 2026)","None","Late morning"],"productTags":["chlebíčky","counter","Dlouhá"],"hours":"Not listed on own site (checked Sept 2026)","why":"Sisters made the office-party chlebíček something to seek out again. The toppings rotate monthly — in September 2026 an eggplant with miso, beside roast beef at 59 Kč and avocado with prosciutto at 62. Buy three, stand at the counter with the house lemonade, and lunch costs under 200 Kč on the street Lokál shares.","address":"Dlouhá, Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.080886,"lng":14.419884,"category":"street","subcat":"LA RUE","hook":"The open sandwich rewritten: roast beef, brie and cranberry, eggplant with miso.","signature":"Roast beef chlebíček, 59 Kč","verdict":"The modern chlebíček counter; the classic ham-and-egg is elsewhere.","caveat":"Standing counter; hours not published, go at lunch.","price_range":"53–65 Kč per chlebíček (own site, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Late morning","dishes":[{"name":"Roast beef","note":"59 Kč"},{"name":"Avocado and prosciutto","note":"62 Kč"},{"name":"Pork tenderloin","note":"56 Kč"},{"name":"Brie with cranberries","note":"53 Kč"},{"name":"September special: eggplant with miso","note":"45–65 Kč range"}],"web":"https://www.sistersbistro.cz/"},
    {"id":"liberske-lahudky","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":48,"name":"Libeřské lahůdky","short":"Libeřské lahůdky","neighborhood":"23 shops across Prague","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Libe%C5%99sk%C3%A9+lah%C5%AFdky+Praha","badge":"LAHŮDKY","tags":["Budget (per-piece prices vary by branch, Sept 2026)","None","Morning"],"productTags":["chlebíčky","family","classic"],"hours":"Branch-dependent (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Jindřiška founded a single shop more than thirty years ago; her son Jiří and his wife Jitka now run 23 across Prague, each assembling its chlebíčky on site. This is the classic register — ham, egg, potato salad, a slice of gherkin, under aspic if you ask — the counter where Prague buys for name days, office birthdays and funerals.","address":"","phone":"+420 703 636 921","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.09012,"lng":14.43492,"category":"street","subcat":"LA RUE","hook":"Ham, egg and potato salad on soft veka: the chlebíček as grandmother made it, in 23 shops.","person":"Founder Jindřiška; now Jiří and Jitka","signature":"Ham-and-egg chlebíček with potato salad","verdict":"The standard against which every new chlebíček is judged.","caveat":"Chain shops vary; buy early before the tray thins.","price_range":"Budget (per-piece prices vary by branch, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Morning","dishes":[{"name":"Chlebíček with ham and potato salad","note":""},{"name":"Chlebíček with egg","note":""},{"name":"Máslová brioška","note":"butter brioche"}],"web":"https://www.liberskelahudky.cz/"},
    {"id":"mysak","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":49,"name":"Myšák","short":"Myšák","neighborhood":"Nové Město · Vodičkova (also Holešovice market and Prague Castle)","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=My%C5%A1%C3%A1k+Vodi%C4%8Dkova+Praha","badge":"1911","tags":["Cukrárna prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","None","Mid-afternoon"],"productTags":["cukrárna","větrník","history"],"hours":"Vodičkova Mon–Fri 8:00–19:00, Sat–Sun 9:00–19:00 (own site, Sept 2026)","why":"Myšák was one of the great Prague confectioners of the First Republic; its Vodičkova shop reopened in 2017 under the pastry chef Lukáš Pohl. The cakes are the Czech canon — větrník, laskonky, chocolate-dipped meringues — cut small on purpose so you can eat several. Branches followed at the Holešovice market in 2025 and Prague Castle in 2026.","address":"Vodičkova, Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.081257,"lng":14.42432,"category":"street","subcat":"LA RUE","hook":"A First Republic confectioner of 1911, back on Vodičkova since 2017, cutting its cakes small.","person":"Head pastry chef Lukáš Pohl","signature":"Větrník","verdict":"The Prague cukrárna done properly, in the centre.","caveat":"The Castle branch is priced for the Castle.","price_range":"Cukrárna prices (not seen, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Mid-afternoon","dishes":[{"name":"Větrník","note":"caramel choux"},{"name":"Laskonky","note":"coconut meringue with butter cream"},{"name":"Chocolate-coated meringue","note":""}],"web":"https://www.mysak.ambi.cz/en/","hot_this_month":"The second Myšák, opened 2025 in Hall 27 of the renovated Holešovice market."},
    {"id":"u-cerneho-vola","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":51,"name":"U Černého vola","short":"Černý vůl","neighborhood":"Hradčany · Loretánské náměstí, opposite the Loreta","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+%C4%8Cern%C3%A9ho+vola+Praha","badge":"PIVNICE","tags":["Local pub prices (not verified Sept 2026)","Walk in; share a table","Late afternoon after the castle"],"productTags":["Kozel","heritage","samizdat"],"hours":"Afternoon to late; check locally","why":"The Black Ox opened as a pivnice in 1965 in a listed house where a tavern is recorded in 1726, and has kept its elbow-polished oak tables, tiles and beams. In the late 1980s it was a drop box for the samizdat Lidové noviny, and part of its takings long supported the Jaroslav Ježek conservatory for blind students nearby.","address":"Loretánské náměstí 1, 118 00 Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.088148,"lng":14.391847,"category":"pubs","subcat":"PUBS & BEER","hook":"A 1965 pub on the castle hill that once hid samizdat and still pays for a school.","signature":"Velkopopovický Kozel 12°","verdict":"The only pub worth your time on the castle hill, and one of the most honest rooms in Prague.","caveat":"Small and often full; very little English spoken, simple food.","price_range":"Local pub prices (not verified Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk in; share a table","best_time":"Late afternoon after the castle","dishes":[{"name":"Kozel 12°","note":"the house beer"},{"name":"Kozel tmavý","note":"dark lager"},{"name":"Utopenci","note":"pickled sausages, bar snack"}]},
    {"id":"u-vystreleneho-oka","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":52,"name":"U Vystřelenýho oka","short":"Oko","neighborhood":"Žižkov · under Vítkov hill and the Žižka statue","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=U+Vyst%C5%99elen%C3%BDho+oka+Praha","badge":"HOSPODA","tags":["Neighbourhood prices (not verified Sept 2026)","Walk in","Evening; garden in summer"],"productTags":["Žižkov","Pilsner","cash only"],"hours":"Afternoon to late; cash only","why":"Opened in 1993 under the hill where Žižka rides in bronze, 'At the Shot-Out Eye' is Žižkov's reference pub: Pilsner, loud music, a summer garden with concerts and readings. The painter Martin Velíšek did the décor — Žižka riding a seahorse, an aquarium in a tap, fake windows onto the battle of Vítkov, and the famous urinal head-rests.","address":"","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","category":"pubs","subcat":"PUBS & BEER","hook":"Žižkov's pub of 1993: Žižka on a seahorse, an aquarium in a tap, and head-rests at the urinals.","person":"Décor by Martin Velíšek","signature":"Pilsner Urquell","verdict":"The pub to understand Žižkov, the district with Prague's most pubs.","caveat":"Smoky, noisy, ironic staff, cash only; the food is not the point.","price_range":"Neighbourhood prices (not verified Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk in","best_time":"Evening; garden in summer","dishes":[{"name":"Pilsner Urquell","note":"the house beer"},{"name":"Nakládaný hermelín","note":"pickled camembert-style cheese"}],"web":"http://www.uvoka.cz/"},
    {"id":"dva-kohouti","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":54,"name":"Dva kohouti","short":"Dva kohouti","neighborhood":"Karlín · a courtyard off Sokolovská","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dva+kohouti+Praha","badge":"BREWPUB","tags":["Not verified Sept 2026","No reservations","Weekday from 17:00"],"productTags":["brewpub","Karlín","courtyard"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 15:00–01:00, Sat 12:00–01:00, Sun 12:00–22:00 (site, Sept 2026)","why":"Brewer Adam Matuška and bartender Lukáš Svoboda founded Dva kohouti — two roosters — and Lukáš Tomsa now brews its twelve-degree pilsner-type lager from Czech malt and Žatec hops, 4.9 per cent, with rotating specials; in February 2026 it bottled its first barrel-aged beer. The courtyard, shared with street-food stalls, is Karlín's evening living room.","address":"Sokolovská 81/55, 186 00 Praha 8","phone":"+420 604 611 001","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.093494,"lng":14.446819,"category":"pubs","subcat":"PUBS & BEER","hook":"A Karlín courtyard brewery whose twelve is drunk metres from the tanks it came from.","person":"Lukáš Tomsa (brewer)","signature":"The house 12° lager","verdict":"The freshest beer-from-the-source experience in central Prague.","caveat":"No bookings; packed on warm evenings.","price_range":"Not verified Sept 2026","reservation":"No reservations","best_time":"Weekday from 17:00","dishes":[{"name":"Dva kohouti 12°","note":"pilsner-type lager, 4.9%"},{"name":"Seasonal specials","note":"rotating, including barrel-aged bottles"}],"web":"https://www.dvakohouti.ambi.cz/en"},
    {"id":"grand-cafe-orient","cat":"berth","tier":"berth_top","priority":3,"name":"Grand Café Orient","short":"Orient","neighborhood":"Staré Město · first floor of the House of the Black Madonna, by the Powder Tower","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Grand+Caf%C3%A9+Orient+Praha","badge":"CUBIST","tags":["Espresso 80 CZK, věneček 95 CZK, cakes 150–195 CZK (menu PDF June 2025, seen Sept 2026)","Walk in","Weekday 9:00–10:30"],"productTags":["cubist","věneček","1912"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 9:00–21:00, Sat–Sun 10:00–21:00 (website, Sept 2026; menu PDF says 22:00)","why":"Josef Gočár designed the café at 31, with the House of the Black Madonna around it: a buffet-bar, brass, lanterns. Cubism fell out of favour and the café closed in the 1920s after about ten years. In 2004 Rudolf Břínek won the space in a ministry tender and rebuilt it from archive photographs; it reopened in 2005, and Focus magazine ranked it among Europe's seven most beautiful cafés.","address":"Ovocný trh 19, Praha 1","phone":"+420 224 224 240","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.087004,"lng":14.425517,"category":"cafe","subcat":"GRAND CAFÉS","hook":"The world's only Cubist café, dark for eighty years, rebuilt from old photographs.","person":"Rudolf Břínek (operator)","signature":"Kubistický věneček with a vídeňská káva","verdict":"The one grand café no other city can give you; go at opening.","caveat":"Tourist traffic from Celetná by late morning; the food is ordinary café fare.","price_range":"Espresso 80 CZK, věneček 95 CZK, cakes 150–195 CZK (menu PDF June 2025, seen Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk in","best_time":"Weekday 9:00–10:30","dishes":[{"name":"Kubistický věneček","note":"Square choux ring with custard cream, 95 CZK"},{"name":"Vídeňská káva","note":"Viennese coffee under whipped cream, 100 CZK"},{"name":"Kubistický punčový dort","note":"Cubist punch cake, 175 CZK"},{"name":"Medový dort","note":"Honey cake, 150 CZK"},{"name":"Grand Cafe Orient káva","note":"Espresso, Havana rum, Kahlúa, cream, 180 CZK"}],"web":"https://grandcafeorient.cz/"},
    {"id":"cafe-louvre","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":57,"name":"Café Louvre","short":"Louvre","neighborhood":"Nové Město · first floor on Národní, between the theatre and Wenceslas Square","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caf%C3%A9+Louvre+Praha","badge":"KAVÁRNA","tags":["Espresso 59 CZK, cappuccino 69 CZK, cakes 79–119 CZK (website, Sept 2026)","Walk in; book for groups","Breakfast or a weekday afternoon"],"productTags":["1902","kafka","billiards"],"hours":"Mon–Fri 8:00–23:30, Sat–Sun 9:00–23:30 (website, Sept 2026)","why":"Café Louvre opened in 1902. Kafka and Max Brod moved in its circle around 1905; Einstein was a regular in 1912, during his year at the German University; and in 1925 the Czechoslovak PEN Club was founded here with President Masaryk as a guest. It still runs the way Praguers use a café: newspapers, a billiard room, a lunch menu.","address":"Národní 22, Praha 1","phone":"+420 724 054 055","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.082067,"lng":14.418731,"category":"cafe","subcat":"GRAND CAFÉS","hook":"The working grand café since 1902: Kafka nearby, Einstein a regular, billiards at the back.","signature":"Vídeňská káva and a Sacher with cream","verdict":"The grand café to actually spend a morning in.","caveat":"Less photogenic than Orient or Obecní dům; the room is plainer than its guest list.","price_range":"Espresso 59 CZK, cappuccino 69 CZK, cakes 79–119 CZK (website, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk in; book for groups","best_time":"Breakfast or a weekday afternoon","dishes":[{"name":"Vídeňská káva","note":"89 CZK"},{"name":"Klasický Sacher se šlehačkou","note":"109 CZK"},{"name":"Tvarohový dort Louvre","note":"House quark cake with peaches, 109 CZK"},{"name":"Domácí buchta s mákem","note":"Poppy-seed bun, 139 CZK"},{"name":"Marie Terezie","note":"Espresso with orange liqueur, 99 CZK"}],"web":"https://www.cafelouvre.cz/"},
    {"id":"kavarna-slavia","cat":"shop","tier":"plenty","priority":58,"name":"Kavárna Slavia","short":"Slavia","neighborhood":"Staré Město · corner of Národní and the embankment, opposite the National Theatre","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kav%C3%A1rna+Slavia+Praha","badge":"KAVÁRNA","tags":["Espresso 88 CZK, vídeňská káva 140 CZK, desserts 202–238 CZK (website, Sept 2026)","Walk in; window tables go first","Late morning or after a theatre performance"],"productTags":["1884","havel","absinthe"],"hours":"Mon–Sat 9:00–23:00, Sun 9:00–22:00 (website, Sept 2026)","why":"Václav Zoufalý opened Slavia in 1884 in the Lažanský Palace; the Art Deco refit came in 1931–32. Smetana, the Čapek brothers and Seifert sat here, and later Havel's circle. Havel kept a window table and campaigned to reopen the café after it closed in the 1990s; it reopened on 17 November 1997. Viktor Oliva's Absinthe Drinker of 1901 hangs inside.","address":"Národní 1, Praha 1","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.081541,"lng":14.413244,"category":"cafe","subcat":"GRAND CAFÉS","hook":"The theatre-and-dissident café opposite the National Theatre, where Havel kept a window table.","signature":"An absinthe beneath the Oliva painting, or a coffee at a river window","verdict":"Pay for the window and the story, not the cake.","caveat":"Among the most expensive coffees in town; the cake list leans to sundaes and pancakes, not the Czech canon.","price_range":"Espresso 88 CZK, vídeňská káva 140 CZK, desserts 202–238 CZK (website, Sept 2026)","reservation":"Walk in; window tables go first","best_time":"Late morning or after a theatre performance","dishes":[{"name":"Vídeňská káva","note":"Filter coffee under whipped cream, 140 CZK"},{"name":"Absinth","note":"Several pours, 145–255 CZK"},{"name":"Domácí závin s jablky","note":"Apple strudel with vanilla sauce, 238 CZK"},{"name":"Pohár Slavia","note":"House sundae, 208 CZK"}],"web":"https://www.cafeslavia.cz/"},
    {"id":"naplavka-farmers-market","cat":"market","tier":"several","priority":61,"name":"Farmářské tržiště Náplavka","short":"Náplavka","neighborhood":"Nové Město · on the Vltava embankment below Palackého náměstí","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Farm%C3%A1%C5%99sk%C3%A9+tr%C5%BEi%C5%A1t%C4%9B+N%C3%A1plavka+Praha","badge":"MARKET","tags":["Market prices; burčák and snacks from about 50-100 CZK (estimate, Sept 2026)","None","8:00-9:30"],"productTags":["farmers","river","saturday"],"hours":"Sat 8:00-14:00, February to December (farmarsketrziste.cz, Sept 2026)","why":"The city's best-known market fills the stone embankment on the Vltava itself every Saturday from February to December: seasonal vegetables, forest mushrooms, pond fish, cheese, eggs, bread, and from August to November burčák poured by the glass. When a big event takes the quay it moves up to Palackého náměstí. The producers are real; the prices are a little higher than Jiřák's.","address":"Rašínovo nábřeží, Praha 2","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.0688,"lng":14.414436,"category":"market","subcat":"THE LARDER","hook":"Ninety stalls on the river embankment every Saturday, with the castle across the water.","signature":"Burčák by the glass in autumn","verdict":"The Saturday ritual worth planning a day off around, if you arrive by 8:30.","caveat":"By noon it is a promenade and the queues are for photographs as much as food.","price_range":"Market prices; burčák and snacks from about 50-100 CZK (estimate, Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"8:00-9:30","dishes":[{"name":"Burčák","note":"Half-fermented must, legal only 1 Aug-30 Nov"},{"name":"Forest mushrooms","note":"Sold by the pickers in season"},{"name":"Smoked and fresh farm cheeses","note":"Bohemian and Moravian dairies"},{"name":"Povidla and honey","note":"Plum butter and forest honey, both travel well"},{"name":"Fresh pond fish","note":"Carp and trout from Czech fisheries"}],"web":"https://www.farmarsketrziste.cz/","hot_this_month":"October 2026 Saturdays: 3, 10, 17, 24, 31."},
    {"id":"jirak-market","cat":"market","tier":"several","priority":62,"name":"Trhy na Jiřáku","short":"Jiřák","neighborhood":"Vinohrady · around Plečnik's church on náměstí Jiřího z Poděbrad","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Trhy+na+Ji%C5%99%C3%A1ku+Praha","badge":"MARKET","tags":["Market prices (Sept 2026)","None","Weekday late afternoon or Saturday morning"],"productTags":["farmers","weekday","vinohrady"],"hours":"Wed-Fri 8:00-18:00, Sat 8:00-14:00 (trhyjirak.cz, Sept 2026)","why":"Jiřák runs four days a week on the square round Jože Plečnik's church, which makes it the one farmers' market you can shop after work. Fruit, vegetables, mushrooms, herbs, teas, eggs, cheese, bread, honey and preserves — smaller and more local than Náplavka, with residents carrying shopping bags rather than visitors carrying phones.","address":"náměstí Jiřího z Poděbrad, Praha 3","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.077964,"lng":14.450349,"category":"market","subcat":"THE LARDER","hook":"Wednesday to Saturday under Plečnik's church: the market Vinohrady actually shops at.","signature":"Weekday produce shopping with the locals","verdict":"The market to use rather than visit.","caveat":"Fewer stalls on weekdays than on Saturday.","price_range":"Market prices (Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Weekday late afternoon or Saturday morning","dishes":[{"name":"Moravian and Bohemian cheeses","note":"Several dairy stalls"},{"name":"Seasonal mushrooms","note":"Whatever was picked that week"},{"name":"Bakers' loaves and pastries","note":"From the bakers' stalls"},{"name":"Honey and preserves","note":"For the sea bag"}],"web":"https://trhyjirak.cz/","hot_this_month":"Sat 10 Oct 2026: reuse and swap day on the square, 10:00-17:00."},
    {"id":"holesovice-hall-22","cat":"market","tier":"several","priority":64,"name":"Holešovická tržnice · Hala 22","short":"Hall 22","neighborhood":"Holešovice · the old slaughterhouse complex by the river","maps":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hole%C5%A1ovick%C3%A1+tr%C5%BEnice+Hala+22+Praha","badge":"HALL","tags":["Wholesale-leaning market prices (Sept 2026)","None","Weekday morning"],"productTags":["vegetables","weekday","holešovice"],"hours":"Mon-Fri 7:30-17:00, Sat 7:30-14:00, Sun closed (holesovickatrznice.cz, Sept 2026)","why":"The Holešovice complex was built in the 1890s as the city slaughterhouse. Hall 22 is its working heart: growers' vegetables, bread, dairy, spices, meat, fish and flowers from more than eighty vendors, six days a week, where restaurant cooks and pensioners shop from the same crates. The rest of the site is outlet stalls and can be skipped.","address":"Bubenské nábřeží 306/13, Praha 7","phone":"","status":"confirmed","statusChecked":"2026-09-27","lat":50.099672,"lng":14.445984,"category":"market","subcat":"THE LARDER","hook":"The city's biggest vegetable market, six days a week, in the halls of the old slaughterhouse.","signature":"Vegetables by the crate","verdict":"The provisioning run that is also a piece of city history.","caveat":"Plain hall, no river view; the surrounding outlet stalls are dispiriting.","price_range":"Wholesale-leaning market prices (Sept 2026)","reservation":"None","best_time":"Weekday morning","dishes":[{"name":"Growers' vegetables","note":"Seasonal, sold in bulk"},{"name":"Dried mushrooms and caraway","note":"The Czech spice rack"},{"name":"Fish","note":"Pond fish in season"},{"name":"Dairy and eggs","note":"Farm producers"}],"web":"https://www.holesovickatrznice.cz/en","hot_this_month":"Closed Mon 28 Sept 2026 (St Wenceslas holiday)."}
