   "story": "Until late 2025 the Czech Republic had no MICHELIN guide of its own. On 11 December 2025, at a ceremony in the spa town of Mariánské Lázně, the Czech Republic got a guide of its own: one two-star, eight one-stars, eighteen Bib Gourmands. Five of the stars landed in Prague. Two were holdovers, Field and La Degustation Bohême Bourgeoise; three were new, Levitate, Štangl and the family-run Italian Casa De Carli. The only two-star went to Papilio, in a village near the Brdy forest. The guide also gave its Service Award to Miroslav Nosek, the owner of Field, for welcoming guests with what the inspectors called remarkable courtesy.",
