   "story": "Most Czech pubs pour from kegs. The tank pub (tankovna) keeps unpasteurised Pilsner Urquell in large tanks and pours it with the shortest possible line. Lokál Dlouhááá opened in 2009 with the tanks directly beneath the taps, and its bartenders are trained to pour three ways: hladinka (a clean head), šnyt (a short pour under a thick collar) and mlíko, a glass of almost nothing but wet foam, drunk in one go. The food followed the same logic: nothing clever, everything made that day. Ask for a mlíko before your svíčková; it is how locals judge a tapster.",
