   "title": "Why the pub is Prague's real restaurant",
   "story": "Czechs drank 121 litres of beer per head in 2025 — a historic low, and still the world's highest for the 32nd year. The beer that made them famous was born 90 km west in Plzeň on 5 October 1842, when a Bavarian brewer mashed the first golden lager with Saaz hops. In Prague the difference between a great pub and a trap is freshness and honesty: tank beer, a proper pour, a pencil tally, and a half-litre at 50–75 CZK rather than 150. The pubs here are chosen for that.",
