   "story": "Café Savoy on Vítězná opened under a painted Neo-Renaissance ceiling that its owners date to 1893. Today the Ambiente group runs it as a Viennese-style café by day and a quieter restaurant by night. The pastries in the morning cabinet are baked with Myšák, the confectioner founded in 1911 on Vodičkova. That connection is the point: Prague breakfast is a café-and-confectioner culture before it is an eggs culture. Order coffee, a pastry from the cabinet and one savoury plate, and look up. Taste of Prague's 2026 solo-dining guide singles out its breakfast among the grand cafés.",
