   "story": "The Czech jídelna, the self-service canteen, is the country's real fast food. At Havelská Koruna you take a paper ticket at the door, the cooks mark what you take, and you pay on the way out: svíčková, goulash, a fried schnitzel, from some forty dishes a day, under 200 Kč each. At Jídelna Světozor, inside the Světozor passage off Wenceslas Square, the daily three-course bundle was 169 Kč on 27 September 2026, with a senior menu at 120 Kč. These rooms serve office workers and pensioners at the same trays. They close mid-afternoon; lunch here is a noon activity, not a late one.",
